missing t0 -> no\nattempt for [t5,t6] -> candidate [t0,t4,t7] -> missing t6 -> no\nattempt for [t7] -> candidate [t0,t4,t5,t6] -> contains both -> accept. items = [t0,t4,t5,t6]. granularity +=1 -> 3.\ng=3, length4, chunks: [t0,t4,t5], [t6]\nattempt [t0,t4,t5] -> candidate [t6] -> missing t0 -> no\nattempt [t6] -> candidate [t0,t4,t5] -> missing t6 -> no\nNo removal, double g = 6 (>4), set g=1.\ng=1: items [t0,t4,t5,t6]\nattempt each:\n[t0] -> candidate [t4,t5,t6] -> missing t0 -> no\n[t4] -> candidate [t0,t5,t6] -> contains both -> accept. items = [t0,t5,t6]. granularity +=1 -> 2.\ng=2: length3, chunks [t0,t5], [t6]\nattempt [t0,t5] -> candidate [t6] -> missing t0 -> no\nattempt [t6] -> candidate [t0,t5] -> missing t6 -> no\nNo removal, double g=4 (>3) set g=1.\ng=1: items [t0,t5,t6]\nattempt [t0] -> missing t0 -> no\n[t5] -> candidate [t0,t6] -> contains both -> accept. items = [t0,t6]. granularity +=1 -> 2.\ng=2: length2, chunk [t0,t6]\nattempt [t0,t6] -> candidate [] -> missing both -> no\nNo removal, double g=4 (>2) set g=1.\ng=1: chunks [t0],[t6]\nattempt [t0] -> candidate [t6] -> missing t0 -> no\nattempt [t6] -> candidate [t0] -> missing t6 -> no\nNo removal at g=1, and granularity is 1, so break.\nFinal items = [\"t0\",\"t6\"]\none_minimal: at the end, g=1 and no removal succeeded, so True.\nAttempts: count of all attempts made: Let's count: \n- At g=2: 2 attempts (first pass)\n- g=3: 3 attempts (2nd pass)\n- g=4: 2 attempts\n- g=1 (after doubling): 6 attempts (for t1,t4,t5,t6,t7? Actually we had 6 items: t0,t1,t4,t5,t6,t7 -> 6 attempts, then accepted t1)\n- g=2: 3 attempts (t0,t4; t5,t6; t7) -> accepted t7\n- g=3: 2 attempts\n- g=1: 4 attempts (t0,t4,t5,t6) -> accepted t4\n- g=2: 2 attempts\n- g=1: 3 attempts (t0,t5,t6) -> accepted t5\n- g=2: 1 attempt\n- g=1: 2 attempts (t0,t6) -> none accepted, break\nTotal attempts = 2+3+2+6+3+2+4+2+3+1+2 = let's sum: 2+3=5, +2=7, +6=13, +3=16, +2=18, +4=22, +2=24, +3=27, +1=28, +2=30 attempts. So attempts=30. That seems